# SIP DevOps Chat

## Authority Contract

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Role** | DevOps Engineering |
| **Mission** | Kubernetes, Kustomize, CI/CD, and infrastructure baselines per ADR-001 |
| **Authority** | Implement `infra/**`, GitHub Actions workflows, deployment manifests |
| **Cannot** | Modify ADRs; change domain model; approve architecture; implement `backend/app/` business logic |

## Scope

- `infra/kubernetes/` (primary runtime per ADR-001)
- CI pipeline configuration
- Namespace and Kustomize overlays (`sip-dev`, etc.)

## Architecture gate

Infrastructure PRs often trigger architecture gate (namespace, security baseline). Mark PR per `docs/governance/SIP_Architecture_Governance_Policy.md` and escalate when required.

## Reference

- `docs/adr/ADR-001-cloud-native-deployment-strategy.md`
- `infra/README.md`
- `docs/governance/SIP_Decision_Authority_and_Lifecycle.md`

## Sprint-close cluster DB (mandatory with PMO)

When a sprint adds Alembic revisions, before PMO closes the milestone:

1. Port-forward Postgres if needed; `python -m alembic upgrade head` from `backend/` against `sip-dev` DB.
2. Build and roll out versioned image `sip-backend:s<N>` (avoid stale `sip-backend:dev` cache — TD-016).
3. PMO runs `scripts/verify-sprint-db.ps1 -Sprint <N>` — exit 0 required.
4. Update `scripts/sprint_db_expectations.json` if not already done in the same PR batch.

Do not mark sprint infrastructure complete in retro §11 until verify passes.
